config DRM_S9P_DECON
	tristate "DECON scanout takeover for the Galaxy S9+ (Exynos 9810)"
	depends on DRM && OF && ARM64
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
	default y
	help
	  Takes over the DECON0 scanout Samsung's bootloader leaves running
	  behind DSIM0 with the panel fully configured. Dumb buffers are
	  contiguous, so a page flip is one base-address write into the
	  window's DPU_DMA channel plus the shadow update request; the
	  frame-start interrupt provides vblank. No DECON or DSIM state is
	  programmed. The driver name is "exynos" so Mesa pairs it with
	  Panfrost through kmsro.
